{#
  How this module names a person, everywhere it names one: the ACCOUNT —
  the human — then, in parentheses, the memberships that account carries
  for the year in question.

      Marie Dupont (Akéla, Baloo)

  `identity` is Service\MemberIdentityService's own shape. That service's
  docblock holds the reasoning; this file only draws it, in one place, so
  a message, a comment, "qui a réagi", "vu par" and the members page can
  never start disagreeing about how the same person is written.

  Both halves are plain escaped text — an account's first/last name and a
  member's totem are personal data, never markup.
#}
<span class="groups-identity fw-semibold">{{ identity.account_name }}</span>
{%- if identity.member_names is not empty %}
    <span class="groups-identity-members text-body-secondary">({{ identity.member_names|join(', ') }})</span>
{%- endif %}
